WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.270
English loves to drop a word.

2
00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:03.570
The film we saw.

3
00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.750
No that, no which.

4
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.360
French never drops it: «le
film que nous avons vu».

5
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.860
Pull that little word out,

6
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.470
and the French sentence falls apart.

7
00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:16.560
Now you want to say the
film I told you about.

8
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.020
What goes in that gap,

9
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.240
and why can't it stay empty?

10
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.430
In this mission, you'll
merge two sentences into one,

11
00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:26.390
and watch a noun turn into a tiny word.

12
00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:29.270
Then you'll join pairs
of sentences in the lab:

13
00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:32.100
a neighbour, a novel, a café.

14
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.970
Your mission: find out why French
never leaves the gap empty,

15
00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.150
and what goes in it.
